cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Applied Unsupervised Learning: reproducible workflows for label-free modelling"
abstract: >-
  A notebook-first applied unsupervised learning project: seventeen
  executed Jupyter notebooks covering segmentation, dimensionality reduction,
  anomaly detection, topic modelling, recommender embeddings, stability
  analysis, consensus and streaming clustering, nonparametric mixtures,
  time-series and graph methods, and deep clustering. They are backed by
  unsup_lab, a typed and tested Python package with deterministic synthetic
  data generators, label-free evaluation and stability tooling, and a
  production layer of CLI, model artifacts and a scoring API.
type: software
